# RockBase NM-CYD-C5 -- a Cheap Yellow Display with an ESP32-C5 behind it.
#
# The first board here with both a screen and dual-band radio: every other
# display board is a plain ESP32 that cannot see 5 GHz at all, and every
# board that can was headless. A sniffer that sweeps both bands and shows
# what it found on its own glass is a combination this project has not had.
#
# 16 MB flash, 8 MB PSRAM, native USB-Serial/JTAG, and the same 2.8" 320x240
# ST7789 panel as the classic CYD -- but almost none of the same pins.
#
# Taken from RockBase's own TFT_eSPI setup and pin header rather than from a
# summary: the first description found gave the display chip select as GPIO3,
# and it is 23.
#
#   ST7789   MISO 2  MOSI 7  SCLK 6  CS 23  DC 24  backlight 25 (active high)
#   XPT2046  shares that bus, CS 1, and its interrupt is not wired at all
#   WS2812   27        BOOT 28        SD card CS 10
#
# The panel's reset is tied to the board's, so there is no pin to drive.
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_DISPLAY=y
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_DISPLAY_ST7789=y
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_DISPLAY_WIDTH=320
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_DISPLAY_HEIGHT=240
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_DISPLAY_MISO=2
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_DISPLAY_MOSI=7
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_DISPLAY_SCLK=6
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_DISPLAY_CS=23
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_DISPLAY_DC=24
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_DISPLAY_RST=-1
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_DISPLAY_BL=25
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_DISPLAY_MHZ=20
# The vendor's setup turns inversion off, against the ST7789 CYDs which need
# it on. Each of these is a build option because the failure it causes is
# distinct and visible: a negative means this one is wrong.
# CONFIG_OBSERVORE_DISPLAY_INVERT is not set
# Red and blue in the host's order, unlike the classic CYDs.
#
# Settled by looking rather than reasoning, and it took two readings because
# each setting alone produces a plausible-looking wrongness. With the swap on
# and BGR on, amber came out blue; with the swap off and BGR on, amber came
# out red and blue came out green. Only a red/blue swap turns amber blue;
# only a byte swap on top of it turns blue into green. So the byte swap was
# already happening in hardware, and asking for one in software was
# cancelling it -- turning it off added a swap rather than removing one.
# CONFIG_OBSERVORE_DISPLAY_BGR is not set
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_DISPLAY_MIRROR_X=y
# CONFIG_OBSERVORE_DISPLAY_MIRROR_Y is not set
# No photoresistor on this board.
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_DISPLAY_LDR_GPIO=-1

# Touch shares the panel's bus, and its interrupt line goes nowhere -- the
# vendor's own pin table prints "---" for it -- so the pressure channels are
# read on every poll and the threshold decides.
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_TOUCH=y
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_TOUCH_XPT2046=y
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_TOUCH_SHARED_BUS=y
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_TOUCH_POLLED=y
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_TOUCH_CS=1
# The bounds below are the defaults rather than measurements from this panel,
# and that is no longer the problem it was: the `calibrate` action on the
# system page measures the sheet in front of the owner and keeps the result in
# NVS. These are a starting point. The crossing is not guessable that way, so
# it is set here -- a left-right press swings raw Y, not raw X.
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_TOUCH_SWAP_XY=y

# The addressable pixel the C5 boards carry, on the same pin as the DevKitC.
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_LED_ADDRESSABLE=y
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_LED_GPIO=27
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_BUTTON_GPIO=28

# Wi-Fi and lwIP buffers out of internal memory, which this board has very
# little of to spare: eleven kilobytes free and a seven kilobyte floor on the
# first run, against fifty on the classic CYD. Eight megabytes of PSRAM sit
# behind it doing nothing.
#
# Deliberately not CONFIG_MBEDTLS_EXTERNAL_MEM_ALLOC: on C5 revision v1.0 the
# chip warns at boot that PSRAM contents are not encrypted, and TLS buffers
# are the one thing that should not go there.
CONFIG_SPIRAM_TRY_ALLOCATE_WIFI_LWIP=y

CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHSIZE_16MB=y
CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHSIZE="16MB"

# A device with a display does not need to push notifications, and leaving
# the notifier out is what keeps the TLS handshake off a board that has a
# screen to say it on.
# CONFIG_OBSERVORE_NOTIFIER is not set

# Half the usual device table, which is 13 KB of internal RAM back.
#
# Measured against the pool allocations actually come from, this board's
# low-water mark was 2,544 bytes over a ten-minute watch, with a 6,144-byte largest
# free block at that point. The device table is the largest single static
# allocation this firmware makes -- 136 bytes a slot, 26 KB at 192 -- and
# PSRAM does not help it, because it is a static array rather than something
# allocated at runtime.
CONFIG_OBSERVORE_MAX_DEVICES=96

CONFIG_OBSERVORE_BOARD="nm-cyd-c5"
